Problem: the Linux Backend (Rust) PR job failed under strict Clippy because a Windows-only test helper import was compiled on every test platform, and the browser Ready-event helper was compiled in a normal Linux library even though production only uses it with native_browser. Objective: restore strict cross-platform CI without weakening warnings or changing runtime behavior. Decisions: gate relative_workspace_path_with with all(test, windows); gate is_browser_ready_event with any(test, native_browser), preserving its tests on every OS and its production use on Windows/macOS while excluding it from the non-native Linux library. Validation: cargo clippy --lib --features windows-tests -- -A dead-code -D warnings passed; cargo test --lib --features windows-tests -- --test-threads=1 passed with 2970 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored; cargo fmt --check passed; git diff --check passed; graphify update . completed. The all-targets + windows-tests combination is intentionally not used because that feature disables the Windows executable entry point while Cargo still tries to compile the binary; library checks match the CI coverage relevant to this change.
